<br/>
A touch sensor is built directly in the display panel, so there is no added latency. Apple says touch interactions feel "incredibly responsive and refined." Users can scroll through a webpage with a swipe, pinch to zoom in on a photo, drag and drop slides from one presentation to another, and double-tap a window to have it fill the screen.<br/>
<br/>
A new hinge design offers more stability when using touch, and advanced video stabilization smooths the camera feed when using touch on a video call. Apple says macOS automatically translates touch into clicks, so many existing apps will work with touch right away. <br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; is up to 1mm slimmer than the existing version, and it is lighter weight at just three pounds for the 14-inch model and four pounds for the 16-inch model. There is no more notch, with Apple instead adding a small <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a> that takes up less space. The &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj; houses Spotlight, Live Activities, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI. Like on the iPhone, it offers a quick way to see and interact with important information. <br/>
<br/>
Smaller bezels mean the 16-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; display is now 16.3 inches in size, while the 14-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; is now 14.2 inches. <br/>
<br/>
The new &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; uses the same M5 Pro and M5 Max chips as the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models announced back in March, but there is a redesigned thermal architecture that directs warm air away from the display. There is support for up to 128GB of unified memory, and a new six-speaker sound system with 50 percent deeper bass.<br/>
<br/>
There are three Thunderbolt 5 ports, HDMI, an SDXC card slot, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/magsafe/">MagSafe</a>, and a headphone jack. The new machines support up to four external displays and come with Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6. Fast charging allows the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; to be charged to 50 percent in 30 minutes, and up to 16TB storage is available. <br/>
<br/>
